' =====================================================================
'  Annotated class diagram — self-contained (single file, no !include).
'
'  Scope: the export/ package — concrete Exporter implementations.
'  The Exporter seam itself moved into core/engine/ (see
'  Class_Diagram/class_diag_commented.puml) once WorldEngine grew its
'  own optional `exporter` field — WorldEngine.advance_time_step()
'  calls exporter.record() directly, no wrapper class needed. export/
'  supplies the concrete side only, the same shape as pibt/ supplying
'  a concrete PathPlanner: depends on core/, core/ does not know it
'  exists. core/ classes referenced here (WorldEngine, Exporter, Agent,
'  Grid2D, StepOutcome) are shown as stubs; see
'  Class_Diagram/class_diag_commented.puml for their real detail.
'
'  Regenerate with:
'      plantuml diagrammes/Class_Diagram/Export/class_diag_commented.puml
'
'  Output:
'      export_class_diagram_commente.png
' =====================================================================

@startuml export_class_diagram_commente
title Simulation — export/ class diagram (annotated: context & design patterns)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ClassBorderColor #4A90D9
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #EAF4FF
skinparam ClassHeaderBackgroundColor #4A90D9
skinparam ClassHeaderFontColor #FFFFFF
skinparam PackageBorderColor #888888
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9B458
skinparam linetype ortho

' =====================================================================
'  core — stubs only; this package's real home is Class_Diagram/
' =====================================================================
package "core (stubs)" #EAF4FF {
    class WorldEngine
    abstract class Exporter
    class Agent
    class Grid2D
    class StepOutcome
}

' =====================================================================
'  export — concrete Exporters; no seam of its own, core owns that now
' =====================================================================
package "export" #FFF3E0 {

    class PlanVizExporter {
        - _history       : dict[int, list[tuple]]
        - _grid          : Grid2D | None
        - _ticks_per_action : int = 1
        --
        + record(step, agents, grid, outcome) : void
        + flush() : void
    }
    note bottom of PlanVizExporter
      **The concrete reason this package exists**
      Accumulates (position, orientation) per agent per tick, one
      baseline entry before the first real tick so the very first
      recorded heading can be treated as "where the agent started"
      rather than an invented rotation from Agent's default NORTH —
      see the worked trace in this session's transcript.

      flush() run-length-encodes the deltas into the Start-Kit's own
      action vocabulary (Simulator.cpp): F (forward), R (rotate
      clockwise), C (rotate counter-clockwise), W (wait) — a same-tick
      position+orientation change (PIBTPlanner's orientation=True
      never enforces rotate-XOR-move) becomes N clockwise-step R/C
      actions followed by one F, N computed from the shortest turn
      between the two Orientations. Row/col are swapped versus this
      project's (x, y): the segment header is (tick, y, x, heading, 0),
      not (tick, x, y, heading, 0) — matches the Start-Kit's own
      row-major (location = row*cols+col) convention, which happens to
      agree with core's own (x East+, y South+) axes once transposed.
      _ticks_per_action defaults to 1 (one PlanViz tick per WorldEngine
      tick) rather than modeling the Start-Kit's agentCounter (~10
      execution ticks per Forward/Rotate) — a deliberate simplification,
      not an oversight; raising it replays every tick N times for more
      realistic pacing in PlanViz's own player.

      Writes the .map + .json pair PlanViz reads. The only concrete
      Exporter today — CsvExporter, SqlExporter are documented future
      siblings, not yet written.
    end note
}

PlanVizExporter --|> Exporter

PlanVizExporter ..> Agent : «reads»
PlanVizExporter ..> Grid2D : «reads»
PlanVizExporter ..> StepOutcome : «reads»

' =====================================================================
'  Page-level legend — the 30-second read.
' =====================================================================
legend bottom left
  **What this diagram covers**
  export/: concrete Exporters plugged into WorldEngine.exporter. A
  caller wanting a logged run constructs
  WorldEngine(grid, planner, exporter=PlanVizExporter(...)) directly —
  no decorator class, WorldEngine already has the slot. Depends only
  on core/ — the same one-directional shape as pibt/ — and knows
  nothing about PIBT or any other concrete PathPlanner.
  There is currently no code behind any of this — see TODO.md.
end legend

@enduml
